Survey Report on Types of Blockchains and Their Real-Time Use Cases
1. Aim
To study different types of blockchain technology and understand their real-time applications in various industries.

2. Introduction
Blockchain is a decentralized digital ledger technology used to store information securely. Data is stored in blocks that are connected to each other using cryptography. Blockchain provides transparency, security, and immutability.

3. Types of Blockchains
1. Public Blockchain
- Open to everyone.
- Anyone can participate in transactions.
- Highly transparent and decentralized.
- Examples: Bitcoin, Ethereum.
Real-Time Use Cases:
- Cryptocurrency transactions.
- Decentralized finance (DeFi).
- NFT marketplaces.

2. Private Blockchain
- Controlled by a single organization.
- Only authorized users can access it.
- Provides privacy and better control.
Real-Time Use Cases:
- Banking systems.
- Company record management.
- Supply chain management.

3. Consortium Blockchain
- Managed by multiple organizations.
- Access is limited to selected members.
- Provides shared control and transparency.
Real-Time Use Cases:
- Banking networks.
- Healthcare data sharing.
- Logistics and supply chains.

4. Hybrid Blockchain
- Combination of public and private blockchains.
- Some information is private, while selected information is public.
- Provides flexibility and security.
Real-Time Use Cases:
- Government records.
- Real estate management.
- Healthcare applications.

